# Issue #5593: an activation that adopts another activation's row, re-binds an
# existing unbound leaf, or recovers its binding is treated as a birth. Its
# replay read nothing the earlier activation wrote, so its live advance passes
# those owned, acknowledged entries unread.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestRebindIsBirth
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a reactivation that binds an existing leaf (an adopt, a re-bind, a recovery) counts as a birth
PERTURBS: Activate

--- FIND
    \* A reactivation never creates the leaf: an adopted row, a re-bind and a
    \* recovery all bind a leaf another activation created (issue #5593).
    /\ UNCHANGED born
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the binding of an existing leaf is decided as a birth.
    /\ born' = [born EXCEPT ![l] = TRUE]
--- END
